WEBVTT

00:02.809 --> 00:04.936
&lt;i>Call now. Operators are standing by.&lt;/i>

00:05.111 --> 00:06.510
Oh. Ooh, ooh, ooh.

00:06.679 --> 00:07.839
What are you doing?

00:08.014 --> 00:09.140
I'm calling them.

00:09.315 --> 00:12.807
Don't you wanna be able to scramble
an egg while it's still in the shell?

00:15.855 --> 00:17.823
Okay, new rule:

00:17.991 --> 00:20.824
You can't drink
while we watch cable television.

00:20.994 --> 00:25.556
You won't say that when you get
a blanket with sleeves for Christmas.

00:30.570 --> 00:32.060
Hi, Jake.

00:34.974 --> 00:37.101
Can I offer you some fruit and cheese?

00:37.277 --> 00:38.642
You can, but I won't eat it.

00:38.811 --> 00:41.041
Oh, okay.

00:41.414 --> 00:43.814
So, what's new? How's your girlfriend?

00:43.983 --> 00:45.951
That's kind of personal, isn't it?

00:47.086 --> 00:48.951
Sorry, I'm just curious.

00:49.122 --> 00:50.749
Why, you writing a book?

00:52.492 --> 00:56.451
&lt;i>Yeah, it's called
The Day Jake's Uncle Kicked His Ass.&lt;/i>

00:56.629 --> 00:58.563
Whatever.

00:58.731 --> 01:02.428
Oh, no, don't go.
We so enjoy your company.

01:04.370 --> 01:05.735
Did I do something wrong?

01:05.905 --> 01:08.396
Yeah, you anthropomorphized him.

01:09.242 --> 01:10.539
What?

01:10.710 --> 01:13.508
It means treating something
that's not human as if it is.

01:14.847 --> 01:16.610
You know, like you do with your cat.

01:16.783 --> 01:19.183
Which, frankly, makes more sense.

01:19.352 --> 01:23.015
- I'm starting to think Jake resents me.
- See? You're still doing it.

01:23.189 --> 01:26.818
Look, you can't take it personal,
he's a teenager.

01:26.993 --> 01:30.793
You know, that awkward stage between
junior high and methadone clinic.

01:31.831 --> 01:33.594
I just wanna get to know him better.

01:33.766 --> 01:36.667
I already know him.
Trust me, you're not missing anything.

01:36.836 --> 01:40.135
Come on. There's gotta be something
underneath that sullen exterior.

01:40.306 --> 01:43.537
Yeah, a D student with a perpetual boner.

01:46.279 --> 01:48.008
Oh. Ooh, ooh, ooh.

01:48.181 --> 01:50.479
Ginsu knives.

01:51.351 --> 01:53.012
&lt;i>Slow ride&lt;/i>

01:54.387 --> 01:57.879
- Kind of like high school, huh?
- I never did this in high school.

01:58.057 --> 01:59.615
Really? Sex in a car?

01:59.792 --> 02:01.191
You're kind of built for it.

02:03.997 --> 02:05.021
Oh.
- Hmm?

02:05.198 --> 02:06.495
What the heck is this?

02:06.666 --> 02:10.466
Oh. Oh, Jake's retainer.
He lost this years ago.

02:10.637 --> 02:12.696
This cost me like $500.

02:13.506 --> 02:14.905
Anyway.

02:15.074 --> 02:18.373
- No, this is not working for me.
- You want another wine cooler?

02:18.578 --> 02:21.274
- I wanna be in a real bed.
- What do you want me to do?

02:21.447 --> 02:22.744
You won't stay at Charlie's.

02:22.915 --> 02:26.146
How can I go back there
after his fiancée called me a tramp?

02:26.319 --> 02:30.380
She didn't mean it. That was just when
she found out you'd slept with Charlie.

02:30.556 --> 02:33.354
- It doesn't bother you, does it?
- Well, yeah, yeah, a bit.

02:33.526 --> 02:36.518
You know, but, you know,
beggars can't be choosers.

02:37.230 --> 02:39.255
And I love you.

02:41.034 --> 02:43.264
No, not here.

02:43.436 --> 02:45.996
Then where?
I'd be happy to go back to your place...

02:46.172 --> 02:49.164
...if you could get past that little incident
with your mother.

02:49.342 --> 02:52.368
Little incident?
I caught you in bed with her.

02:52.545 --> 02:55.571
Boy, you are just gonna keep
harping on that, aren't you?

02:56.115 --> 02:57.673
Why don't we just go to a hotel?

02:58.184 --> 03:00.709
Well, we could,
but wouldn't that feel kind of cheap?

03:01.220 --> 03:03.313
I'll tell you what feels kind of cheap,
you.

03:03.489 --> 03:05.480
- What are you doing?
- Getting out of here.

03:05.658 --> 03:08.092
- What, you're gonna walk home?
- It's not far, Alan.

03:08.261 --> 03:10.923
You didn't wanna waste the gas,
remember?

03:11.531 --> 03:13.692
- Pardon me for being green.
- Ugh. Goodbye.

03:13.866 --> 03:16.562
Oh, come on, Melissa.
Let's not ruin a beautiful evening.

03:16.736 --> 03:20.035
I already broke the seal
on the condom.

03:20.206 --> 03:22.231
All right, all right, all right.

03:22.408 --> 03:23.705
You win. You win.

03:23.876 --> 03:26.538
I'll take you to a cheap motel.

03:30.817 --> 03:31.909
Oh, great.

03:32.085 --> 03:35.577
Stand and put your hands behind your head.

03:35.755 --> 03:37.017
I can explain.

03:37.190 --> 03:39.454
Hands behind your head!

03:40.860 --> 03:42.521
This is not what it looks like.

03:42.695 --> 03:46.563
I was just chasing this girl
who jumped out of my car...

03:48.000 --> 03:49.729
Oh.

04:30.243 --> 04:32.609
- You got a minute?
- I'm practicing.

04:33.413 --> 04:35.677
Yeah, well, take a pause for the cause.

04:35.882 --> 04:37.315
What?

04:37.817 --> 04:40.115
- Take five.
- Five what?

04:41.521 --> 04:43.887
Just shut up and listen to me.

04:45.892 --> 04:47.951
- You have a problem with Chelsea?
- No.

04:48.127 --> 04:50.322
- So, what's with the attitude?
- What attitude?

04:50.496 --> 04:53.624
I just don't consider fruit and cheese
an acceptable snack.

04:54.167 --> 04:55.725
I don't care. You were rude.

04:55.902 --> 04:59.030
- Kettle corn, that's a snack.
- That's not the point.

04:59.205 --> 05:01.639
Nachos, that's a proper use of cheese.

05:01.808 --> 05:03.469
All right. All right, listen to me.

05:03.643 --> 05:07.238
You're hurting Chelsea's feelings.
I need you to make an effort to be nicer.

05:07.413 --> 05:10.678
Hey, it's not my problem
if your girlfriend's oversensitive.

05:10.850 --> 05:12.715
Yeah, it kind of is.

05:12.919 --> 05:15.683
If you guys can't get along,
then one of you has gotta go.

05:15.855 --> 05:19.018
- Guess who that's gonna be.
- Why, just because you sleep with her?

05:19.192 --> 05:22.025
Good for you.
Why do people think you're stupid?

05:23.296 --> 05:26.322
Because of my grades.
Actually, I'm an underachiever.

05:30.503 --> 05:33.165
- Just be nice to Chelsea, all right?
- Fine.

05:46.853 --> 05:49.515
Well, that was uncalled for.

05:51.524 --> 05:54.220
Just FYI, your son's a moron.

05:54.760 --> 05:57.695
- No, he's an underachiever.
- Where have you been?

05:57.864 --> 05:59.832
- Had a date with Melissa.
- How did it go?

05:59.999 --> 06:03.662
She broke up with me, and I may
have to register as a sex offender.

06:04.837 --> 06:06.270
Well, as long as you had fun.

06:06.439 --> 06:09.772
Do you have any idea how difficult
it is to maintain a relationship...

06:09.976 --> 06:11.443
...when you don't have a place?

06:11.611 --> 06:14.444
If I didn't have a place of my own,
I'd be worried about...

06:14.614 --> 06:16.775
...more important things
than a relationship.

06:16.983 --> 06:19.952
Like, you know,
getting a place of my own.

06:20.486 --> 06:23.512
So you're saying
I'm not entitled to a relationship?

06:24.223 --> 06:25.349
No.

06:25.525 --> 06:29.757
I'm saying if you can't afford dog food,
you don't get a dog.

06:30.263 --> 06:32.493
Oh, great.
So I'm just supposed to be alone?

06:32.665 --> 06:35.634
No, you're supposed to get
your own freaking place.

06:38.404 --> 06:41.567
Just because you keep saying it
doesn't mean it's gonna happen.

06:46.379 --> 06:47.869
How's the French toast, Jake?

06:48.047 --> 06:51.210
It's bread dipped in eggs,
you can't really screw it up.

06:53.519 --> 06:54.577
It's fine.

06:57.023 --> 07:01.289
It's the best damn French toast
I've ever had in my whole frigging life.

07:01.460 --> 07:03.758
Now stop kicking me.

07:04.597 --> 07:07.532
- Okay, guys, I'll see you later.
- You're working on a Sunday?

07:07.700 --> 07:10.100
Well, kind of. Since my brother and I...

07:10.269 --> 07:13.170
...are both extremely anxious for me
to get my own place...

07:13.339 --> 07:15.739
Me, because I'd like
a sense of autonomy...

07:15.908 --> 07:18.638
...and him, because he's a spiteful turd.

07:19.378 --> 07:21.778
- I have found a way
to earn some extra money.

07:21.948 --> 07:24.610
Great. Put me down
for three boxes of Thin Mints...

07:24.784 --> 07:26.445
...and some Peanut Butter Sandies.

07:28.020 --> 07:30.716
Oh. Girl Scout Cookies?
I like those Samoas.

07:31.657 --> 07:34.820
- I'm not selling cookies, Jake.
- Oh.

07:34.994 --> 07:38.054
Then what are you selling?
Better not be your liver. I got dibs.

07:39.265 --> 07:42.291
Hello? Where is my new assistant?

07:43.502 --> 07:45.299
Oh, you didn't.

07:45.471 --> 07:47.462
Morning, all. Here, darling, put this on.

07:47.640 --> 07:49.198
Oh, snazzy. Do I get to keep it?

07:49.375 --> 07:52.401
No. But if this works out,
I'll sell it to you at cost.

07:54.013 --> 07:56.573
- You're working for Mom?
- What else am I supposed to do?

07:56.749 --> 07:59.718
I don't know, some job
that lets you keep your self-respect.

07:59.885 --> 08:01.819
Like, you know, man whore...

08:03.723 --> 08:04.985
...dog dewormer...

08:06.425 --> 08:09.087
...outhouse inspector.
- Morning, Charlie.

08:09.261 --> 08:12.822
Hey, Mom, how are you?
Laxative tester, horse inseminator.

08:13.466 --> 08:16.765
I'm gonna work with Mom and she's
gonna give me a piece of the action.

08:16.936 --> 08:20.531
No, I said having an assistant
would give me a little peace...

08:20.706 --> 08:23.174
...so I could get some action.

08:28.614 --> 08:29.842
Well, whatever, it's a start.

08:30.016 --> 08:33.383
- Let's go.
- No, dear, I say "let's go."

08:33.853 --> 08:36.048
- Oh. Oh, okay.
- Let's go.

08:36.222 --> 08:38.622
Oh, stop. Take my bag.

08:39.358 --> 08:41.189
Now let's go.

08:42.895 --> 08:44.590
This is gonna be fun.

08:46.732 --> 08:48.666
Okay, I'm done.

08:50.770 --> 08:51.964
He didn't say thank you.

08:52.772 --> 08:54.933
He's leaving the room,
we should thank him.

08:58.711 --> 09:03.410
Jake, come back in here
and say thank you to Chelsea.

09:07.353 --> 09:09.844
Jake, I'm warning you.

09:11.691 --> 09:13.591
Jake!

09:17.296 --> 09:19.560
Thank you, Chelsea.

09:24.403 --> 09:26.871
Now, was that so hard?

09:31.010 --> 09:33.774
Oh. Welcome. Welcome.
Please sign in, take a flier.

09:33.946 --> 09:36.779
- There's juice and cookies in the kitchen.
Thank you.

09:36.949 --> 09:40.612
I know, you think you'd never use
a bidet, but trust me...

09:40.786 --> 09:44.950
...once you do,
you'll never go back to just wiping.

09:46.058 --> 09:49.926
Anyway, if you're not ready to buy,
the owners are willing to lease.

09:50.096 --> 09:51.154
Thank you.

09:52.798 --> 09:56.256
You're very welcome. Thanks for coming.

09:56.435 --> 09:59.768
Oh, the rat bastards
live right across the street.

10:01.307 --> 10:03.468
They probably just came
for the free cookies.

10:04.777 --> 10:06.768
Uh, Mom, I have to go to the bathroom.

10:06.946 --> 10:09.107
Number one or number two?

10:09.281 --> 10:11.181
What difference does it make?

10:11.350 --> 10:13.511
Alan, I'm trying to sell a house here.

10:13.719 --> 10:17.280
Warm cookie smell, good.
Hot poop smell, bad.

10:19.625 --> 10:22.116
- I'll wait.
- You're damn right you'll wait.

10:22.294 --> 10:24.785
So the people who own this
live mostly in New York?

10:24.964 --> 10:28.491
Have homes all over the place. Probably
don't remember they have this one.

10:28.667 --> 10:29.998
Hardly seems fair.

10:30.169 --> 10:32.069
You want fair, go live on a kibbutz.

10:32.938 --> 10:34.030
Funny.

10:34.240 --> 10:36.731
How does that work exactly?
Do you have to be Jewish?

10:37.510 --> 10:40.035
Oh. Uh, welcome, welcome.
Please sign in.

10:40.246 --> 10:42.476
There's juice and cookies in the kitchen.

10:51.290 --> 10:53.281
Loose floorboard.

10:57.196 --> 10:58.356
Okay.

10:58.531 --> 11:00.726
We need to talk
about your kid and my fiancée.

11:00.900 --> 11:04.961
I already talked to him and he promised
to stay out of her underwear drawer.

11:05.304 --> 11:06.862
What?

11:07.473 --> 11:10.271
Not that he ever went into it.
Just a precaution.

11:11.877 --> 11:13.208
I don't think you realize...

11:13.379 --> 11:16.212
I would love to have this conversation,
but I gotta work.

11:16.382 --> 11:18.145
- It's 9:00.
- Tell that to our mother.

11:18.317 --> 11:21.514
People wanna see a house at night,
guess who has to show the house.

11:21.687 --> 11:24.178
Well, fine, at least
take the rhesus monkey with you.

11:24.356 --> 11:26.916
Heh, oh, yeah. Nothing sells
a multimillion-dollar home...

11:27.092 --> 11:30.493
...more than a 15-year-old boy
with greasy hair and BO.

11:31.297 --> 11:35.028
Okay, let him stand on the lawn
in a jockey costume, holding a lantern.

11:35.201 --> 11:39.103
You're the one who said I needed to get
my own place. This is what I gotta do.

11:39.305 --> 11:40.567
You don't fool me.

11:40.739 --> 11:43.435
You're never leaving. Never.

11:45.211 --> 11:46.508
That's it.

11:46.679 --> 11:48.943
I'm done trying with that kid.

11:53.919 --> 11:57.116
&lt;i>When did my life turn into
Leave It to Beaver?&lt;/i>

11:59.592 --> 12:02.561
&lt;i>It was more fun
when it was Leave It to Beaver.&lt;/i>

12:03.729 --> 12:05.822
Okay, numbnuts,
what did you say to Chelsea?

12:05.998 --> 12:07.966
- Nothing.
- Then why is she so upset?

12:08.133 --> 12:09.964
I don't know. Maybe it's her period.

12:10.135 --> 12:12.330
She says it wasn't,
but I don't believe her.

12:33.592 --> 12:36.459
Welcome to our love nest,
my tiny sparrow.

12:44.837 --> 12:46.668
This is unbelievable.

12:46.839 --> 12:48.238
How can you afford it?

12:48.407 --> 12:51.171
Well, I didn't buy it, of course.
I'm renting.

12:51.343 --> 12:54.676
I don't get it. Just the other day
we were gonna do it in your car...

12:54.847 --> 12:57.873
...because you didn't wanna shell out
$59 for a hotel room.

12:58.050 --> 13:01.542
It was 69, but this is different.

13:01.720 --> 13:04.848
I get a tax break on it.
You know, the home office.

13:05.024 --> 13:07.390
So you've moved out of
your brother's house?

13:07.560 --> 13:10.654
Uh, well, not quite yet.
This is just a pied-à-terre.

13:10.829 --> 13:14.390
Besides, I might flip it
and move up to something a little bigger.

13:14.567 --> 13:16.034
But you said you're renting.

13:17.236 --> 13:21.764
Yes, yes.
I'm renting with, uh, an option to flip.

13:23.409 --> 13:26.503
But let's not talk money...

13:26.679 --> 13:27.805
...let's talk love.

13:31.350 --> 13:32.942
Shall we go try out the bed?

13:33.652 --> 13:37.281
The bed? With the sheets?

13:37.456 --> 13:40.289
Uh... Beds are so bourgeois,
don't you think?

13:40.793 --> 13:42.784
Oh, Alan. The couch?

13:43.228 --> 13:47.688
Uh, actually, I was thinking right here...

13:47.866 --> 13:49.390
...in front of the fireplace...

13:50.235 --> 13:52.465
...on this beach towel.

13:56.775 --> 13:59.209
Come on, I was trying to be nice.

13:59.378 --> 14:02.108
By asking her if she was on her period?

14:02.281 --> 14:04.943
I was taking an interest.
- You're an idiot.

14:05.117 --> 14:08.314
Why are you making it personal?
I'm not making it personal.

14:10.689 --> 14:14.489
Okay, here's the deal. You two are gonna
stay in here and work this thing out...

14:14.693 --> 14:17.526
...until you're either getting along
or one of you is dead.

14:18.063 --> 14:19.928
FYI, she can kick your ass.

14:22.001 --> 14:23.434
Have fun.

14:28.240 --> 14:31.300
- Hey.
- Hey.

14:33.078 --> 14:36.138
So I guess you owe me an apology.

14:41.153 --> 14:42.780
- Wow.
- Ha, ha.

14:42.955 --> 14:45.480
I've never seen you so forceful and virile.

14:45.658 --> 14:47.250
Oh, thank you, thank you.

14:47.426 --> 14:49.257
You were wonderful too.

14:49.428 --> 14:51.794
You're still on the towel, right?

14:52.965 --> 14:54.023
You know what I think?

14:54.199 --> 14:57.794
Finally making love in a place of our own
has given you more confidence.

14:57.970 --> 15:02.134
Well, truth be told,
I do feel kind of cocky, ha, ha.

15:02.307 --> 15:03.831
No pun intended. Ha, ha.

15:04.009 --> 15:05.670
- Oh, it is so intended.
- You got me.

15:07.046 --> 15:09.606
Yes, I do. Mm.

15:11.517 --> 15:14.452
I wanna make love to you
in every room in this house.

15:14.620 --> 15:18.181
I don't see any reason why not,
as long as we bring the towel.

15:19.758 --> 15:22.386
Of course, we're gonna have to wait
about a half-hour...

15:22.561 --> 15:26.691
...give my erectile medication a chance
to overcome my antidepressants.

15:27.833 --> 15:29.824
You're a complicated man, Alan Harper.

15:30.335 --> 15:32.064
And I've got the medicine chest
to prove it.

15:34.373 --> 15:37.672
- Whoopsie.
- Oh, damn it.

15:37.843 --> 15:38.867
Uh, sorry.

15:39.044 --> 15:41.342
Aah. Sorry doesn't get out the stain.

15:41.513 --> 15:43.845
- Don't you have any club soda?
- How would I know?

15:44.016 --> 15:46.177
Don't rub! Blot, blot, blot!

15:46.351 --> 15:48.581
- Stop yelling at me.
- Just get out of the way.

15:48.787 --> 15:51.119
- What is wrong with you?
- Well, nothing, I ju...

15:54.893 --> 15:56.155
That's your whoopsie.

15:57.696 --> 15:58.924
My mother's gonna kill me.

15:59.098 --> 16:01.066
What does your mother
have to do with it?

16:01.233 --> 16:04.293
Are you kidding?
She doesn't even let me poop here.

16:10.375 --> 16:12.343
Hey, so how did everything work out?

16:12.878 --> 16:13.936
Sit down, Charlie.

16:15.180 --> 16:17.648
- Why?
- Just sit.

16:19.384 --> 16:21.011
Okay.

16:22.855 --> 16:24.322
What's going on?

16:24.490 --> 16:26.788
We figured out
what the problem is between us.

16:26.959 --> 16:28.256
Great. What is it?

16:28.427 --> 16:29.951
You.

16:30.129 --> 16:32.063
Well, this ought to be good.

16:32.698 --> 16:34.928
You told Jake
that he should be nice to me...

16:35.100 --> 16:36.727
...because I was oversensitive?

16:37.569 --> 16:40.732
Well, I don't know
that I said those actual words.

16:40.906 --> 16:44.740
And you called me a D student
with a perpetual you-know-what.

16:44.910 --> 16:46.605
Boner.

16:46.779 --> 16:48.406
Yeah, those were my actual words.

16:49.715 --> 16:51.774
Charlie, don't you see
how you're the one...

16:51.950 --> 16:54.441
...who's been driving a wedge
between us?

16:54.620 --> 16:56.451
No, not really.

16:56.622 --> 16:58.089
I told you he wouldn't get it.

16:59.424 --> 17:01.654
Hang on a second, hang on.

17:01.860 --> 17:04.761
You're blaming me because you two
can't get along and now...

17:07.299 --> 17:08.630
You're right.

17:08.801 --> 17:09.893
You're right.

17:10.068 --> 17:11.228
I'm the problem.

17:11.403 --> 17:13.803
I am so sorry. It won't ever happen again.

17:14.606 --> 17:16.904
- Thank you.
- Thanks.

17:24.316 --> 17:26.341
"Perpetual" means pointy, right?

17:33.458 --> 17:37.087
Okay, I think I got it all out.

17:37.763 --> 17:38.787
You didn't have to yell.

17:40.165 --> 17:42.895
I know, I'm sorry.
I don't know what got into me.

17:43.435 --> 17:45.835
- It was just an accident.
- I know.

17:46.004 --> 17:47.494
You hurt my feelings.

17:48.407 --> 17:50.967
Again, I am so sorry.

17:53.212 --> 17:54.804
Come here.

18:08.927 --> 18:14.194
Now wait till you see the panoramic city
to ocean views at night.

18:20.439 --> 18:21.463
Why are we running?

18:21.640 --> 18:23.904
- Remember I told you I rented this house?
- Yeah.

18:24.076 --> 18:25.100
I lied.

18:28.480 --> 18:30.710
Oh, no, not again.

